{
  // THE DEV-TOOLING PROJECT (D481).
  //
  // WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Until D481 `tsc -b` typechecked NOTHING outside
  // `src`: every project's `include` was `["src"]` or `["vite.config.ts"]`, so
  // 15 of the repo's 712 TypeScript files — the whole mutation corpus, every
  // instrument, both instrument gates, the runner, and three files under
  // `apps/` and `packages/` — were checked by no typechecker at all. D480
  // proved it with a live witness rather than by inspection: a declared
  // survivor's reason keyed `survives.why` where the runner reads
  // `survives.reason`, and it shipped GREEN through `bun run check`, surfacing
  // only when a probe printed `undefined`.
  //
  // ⚠️ THE COST WAS NEVER "an error slips through" — it was WHICH TOOL FINDS
  // IT. With `scripts/` outside the typechecker the mutation sweep was the sole
  // guard over the region, and the sweep is a ~2.7-hour instrument that runs
  // once per slice where `tsc` runs in seconds. A coverage hole in a fast tool
  // is a cost multiplier on the slow one.
  //
  // ⚠️ THIS FILE IS NOT THE FIX. A tsconfig with nothing checking it is exactly
  // the defect this slice exists to close, one level up: the next config edit
  // that drops `scripts` out of `include`, or drops this project out of
  // `tsconfig.json`'s `references`, would restore the hole in silence. So the
  // claim is a COMMAND — `scripts/typecheck-coverage.ts`, `bun run
  // typecheck:coverage`, a step of `bun run check` (D212's precedent, D465's
  // rule).
  //
  // ⚠️ WHY IT IS NOT A PROJECT REFERENCE ON `packages/engine`. The instruments
  // import ENGINE SOURCES by relative path (`../packages/engine/src/effects`),
  // not through the `@luminous/engine` entry point, and `tsc -b` can only route
  // that through a reference if the referenced project is `composite` and emits
  // declarations. `packages/engine` is `noEmit` and deliberately so. Ordinary
  // module resolution pulls those sources into THIS program instead, which
  // typechecks them a second time — measured at a few seconds, and the price of
  // not turning the engine into an emitting project for the sake of a dev tool.
  //
  // ⚠️ `types: ["node"]` rather than the `[]` the app projects use: these are
  // Bun/Node programs and every one of them reaches for `node:fs` or `process`.
  // Bun's own globals are shimmed in `scripts/bun-runtime.d.ts` — see there for
  // why that is a shim and not `@types/bun`.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": [
    "scripts",
    "apps/api/scripts",
    "packages/schema/scripts",
    "apps/api/drizzle.config.ts"
  ]
}
